53,"""The name of the class or property that that has been transformed into the data model entity/attribute/relationship. By convention OWL names are Camel Case.  For example: Joint Stock Company = JointStockCompany
Names in OWL 2 are IRIs, often written in a shorthand prefix:localname, where prefix: is a prefix name that expands to an IRI, and localname is the remainder of the name.""

 ------ 
Original FIB-DM Label = enttLocalName",0
